1. Project Overview
The University Teacher Meeting Management System (UTMMS) is a centralized web-based platform designed to digitize and simplify meeting management activities within a university.
The system will provide an integrated environment where university administrators, department heads, meeting organizers, administrative officers, and teachers can organize, schedule, conduct, and manage academic and administrative meetings.
Traditional university meeting arrangements often depend on phone calls, messaging applications, emails, and spreadsheets. These disconnected communication methods can create scheduling conflicts, communication delays, difficulties in managing attendance, and challenges in maintaining official meeting records.
UTMMS will address these problems through a centralized platform that combines meeting management, teacher availability, smart scheduling, digital invitations, attendance tracking, meeting documentation, and decision management.
An important feature of UTMMS will be its integrated online audio and video meeting functionality.
Teachers will be able to join scheduled meetings directly from the website without requiring a separate video conferencing application. Participants will be able to communicate through their microphones and cameras, view other participants, and participate in real-time academic discussions.
The platform will support both physical and online meetings, providing a unified meeting management experience.
The primary objective is to make university meeting administration more organized, transparent, accessible, and efficient.
