Important Technical Approach:
The online communication system will use WebRTC technology for real-time audio and video transmission.
A Selective Forwarding Unit (SFU), such as LiveKit, will manage multi-participant audio/video streams efficiently.
Socket-based real-time communication will support meeting signaling and room-related events where required.
The server will generate secure, time-limited meeting access tokens after verifying the user's identity, meeting invitation, and permissions.
A STUN/TURN configuration will help establish connections across different networks and restrictive NAT environments.
The proposed architecture will support:
•	One-to-one audio/video communication.
•	Multi-participant university meetings.
•	Screen sharing.
•	Secure meeting room access.
•	Audio-only participation.
