6. Complete System Workflows
6.1 Meeting Creation and Scheduling Workflow
1.	Organizer logs into the system.
2.	Organizer selects Create Meeting.
3.	Organizer enters meeting details.
4.	Selects meeting type: Physical, Online, or Hybrid.
5.	Selects faculty, department, and participants.
6.	Proposes meeting dates and times.
7.	System checks participant availability.
8.	System identifies conflicts and recommends suitable slots.
9.	Organizer selects and confirms a schedule.
10.	For online meetings, the system generates a secure meeting room.
11.	Invitations are sent to participants.
12.	Teachers accept, reject, or request schedule changes.
13.	Organizer reviews participant responses.
14.	Meeting is finalized.
6.2 Online Meeting Workflow
1.	Organizer opens the scheduled meeting.
2.	Organizer selects Start Meeting.
3.	The system activates the meeting room.
4.	Invited teachers receive meeting notifications.
5.	Participants select Join Meeting.
6.	The browser requests microphone and camera permissions.
7.	Participants enter the meeting room.
8.	The system establishes WebRTC connections.
9.	Participants communicate through audio and video.
10.	Participants can mute microphones, disable cameras, or share screens.
11.	The organizer manages meeting participants.
12.	The system records joining and leaving events.
13.	Organizer ends the meeting.
14.	Meeting attendance information is saved.
6.3 Meeting Execution and Documentation Workflow
1.	Participants access meeting information.
2.	Organizer records or verifies attendance.
3.	Meeting agenda is discussed.
4.	Organizer records important discussions.
5.	Meeting decisions are documented.
6.	Action items are assigned.
7.	Meeting minutes are prepared.
8.	Minutes are published.
9.	Participants receive notifications.
6.4 Post-Meeting Workflow
1.	Teachers access published meeting minutes.
2.	Assigned teachers view their responsibilities.
3.	Teachers update task progress.
4.	Department heads monitor progress.
5.	Completed activities are recorded.
6.	Historical meeting reports remain available.
