Infrastructure Considerations
Real-time video and audio require additional server resources and network bandwidth.
The required infrastructure will depend on:
•	Number of simultaneous meetings.
•	Participants per meeting.
•	Video resolution.
•	Audio/video bitrate.
•	Screen-sharing usage.
•	Network conditions.
•	Whether LiveKit is self-hosted or managed.
The production deployment must include an appropriately configured UDP media path and TURN fallback where necessary. HTTPS alone is not sufficient for reliable real-time media connectivity.
