18. Conclusion
The University Teacher Meeting Management System (UTMMS) aims to modernize university meeting administration through a centralized, secure, and responsive digital platform.
By integrating university administration, teacher availability, smart scheduling, invitations, real-time audio and video communication, attendance tracking, documentation, and decision management, the system will provide a complete environment for academic collaboration.
The integrated online meeting functionality will allow teachers to communicate directly through the platform, reducing dependency on separate conferencing applications and keeping meeting activities within a unified management system.
The proposed modular architecture, MongoDB database, Next.js frontend, and WebRTC-based communication infrastructure will provide a foundation for future expansion.
The final objective is to develop a comprehensive university meeting management platform that connects academic staff, simplifies administrative responsibilities, and improves communication and collaboration across the university.

